  "body": "## What changed\n\n- `contour_comp::door` (`crates/motion/src/machining2d/contour_comp.rs`) refuses a 2D Contour under control or wear compensation when the entry or the level transition is Ramp or Helix. The refusal names the mode and the arm, for example: \"control compensation does not ride a Ramp entry - its descent runs on the lead-in and the ring before G41/G42 engages, so the register does not apply to it; pick the Plunge or Arc entry, or Computer compensation\".\n- The rule applies to the wall side and to the bore side. It is checked from the parameters, before any geometry.\n- Computer compensation is unchanged.\n- Decision: `docs/decisions/3888-ramp-comp-refusal.md`. The refusal was chosen over a ramp inside the G41/G42 span (a new span shape and proof) and over a ramp on the lead-in only (its last leg still touches the wall under G40).\n\n## Why\n\nG41/G42 engages on the lead-in move that lands on the ring. The wall-side zig-zag (PR #3833) and the bore side's zig-zag, orbit and dive links run before that move, under G40, at the nominal centre. A register larger than the nominal radius, or a positive wear value, cut the finished wall there, and the verifier did not see it.\n\n## Pinning tests (red on main, green here)\n\n- `crates/motion/tests/machining2d.rs` `a_ramp_or_helix_under_control_or_wear_is_refused_by_name_on_both_sides`: Control and Wear; Side::Outside and Side::Inside (bore); Ramp and Helix entry; Ramp transition. Each is refused by name. Plunge still generates its spans. Red on main: the generation succeeded.\n- `crates/app/tests/control_comp.rs` `a_ramp_or_helix_before_g41_under_control_or_wear_is_refused_and_posts_nothing`: through `GenerateOperation`, Control and Wear, Outside and Auto, Ramp and Helix. Each is refused by name, no toolpath is stored, and the post gate writes no G41/G42 program. Red on main: the generation succeeded.\n- Computer compensation is unchanged: `a_wall_side_ramp_in_computer_compensation_is_unchanged` (motion: the same moves as the default ramp, no span) and `a_wall_side_ramp_in_computer_posts_its_ramp_without_comp_words` (app: the zig-zag stands, and the Fanuc post writes no G41/G42).\n\n## Gates\n\n- `cargo xtask gate quick --base origin/main` (CAMCRAFT_GATE_JOBS=6): 18 steps, 0 failed, 0 stalled. This includes the motion suites `lib`, `climb_direction`, `contour_start_comp`, `control_comp`, `machining2d`, `wear_comp`, and the app suites `control_comp` and `example_catalog*`.\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-motion -p camcraft-app --all-targets -- -D warnings`: clean.\n- Heavy: the touched test binaries have no `#[ignore]` heavy tests, so no targeted heavy step applies. The full heavy lanes were not run.\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- The app pin does not cover Side::Inside: a whole-model source refuses Side::Inside before generation. The door reads only the parameters, so the motion pin holds the bore side.\n- The bore side's Plunge and Arc entries, and the wall side's Arc entry, still run before G41/G42 at the nominal radius. Their dive at the lead-in start or their arc in the air was not changed and was not measured against a register over the nominal radius.\n\nChangelog: A 2D Contour under control or wear compensation now refuses a Ramp or Helix entry (or level transition) by name; the ramp ran on the ring before G41/G42 engaged and could cut the wall.\n\nEffort: high (no escalation)\n\nFixes #3888\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
